{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":71340,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"6b79fe2e-5ac2-55b0-b56e-923ff2c7e43d","total_cost_usd":0.555714,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9685,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7152,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9685,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7152,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9685},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4304,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0043939999999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7152,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9685,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.55132,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-j1-reviewer-fable-44\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:68ab4a740a5628e5849f\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure\",\"bounded_statement\":\"Within the supplied files, the report's selected result (two-sample Student t-test, t(10) = 3.0000, p = 0.0133, 95% CI 0.7719 to 5.2281, declared statistically significant at alpha = 0.05) is obtained by entering all 12 nubbin rows as independent observations, even though the data description designates colony_id as the independent unit and states that the two rows per colony are repeated measurements of the same coral. Re-running the same comparison on the 6 colony means (the authorized independent units, n = 3 per regime) preserves the mean difference of 3.000 mg CaCO3 g^-1 d^-1 but gives t(4) ≈ 2.078, p ≈ 0.106, 95% CI ≈ -1.01 to 7.01, so the report's significance conclusion is not supported at the declared unit of independence.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow pools rows purely by thermal_regime (rates_by_regime iterates over every CSV record and appends each nubbin's rate) and passes these row-level vectors directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind, a procedure that assumes each entry is an independent observation. The colony_id column is read only to tally rows per colony for reporting, never to aggregate or model the within-colony dependence, so each of the 6 independent units (colonies) enters the row-independent t-test twice, inflating the effective sample size from 6 to 12 and the degrees of freedom from 4 to 10.\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description names colony_id as the independent-unit column and states one row is a single nubbin measurement from a parent colony.\",\"observed_value\":\"Independent unit column: colony_id\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":26,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one nubbin's net calcification measurement, taken from one parent colony\\nIndependent unit column: colony_id\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description explicitly warns that rows sharing a colony label are dependent repeated measurements, with treatment applied at the colony level.\",\"observed_value\":\"two nubbins per colony share genotype and tank; rows with the same colony label are repeated measurements of the same coral\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":14,\"quoted_text\":\"The temperature treatment was applied to whole colonies, and the two nubbins from\\na colony share that colony's genotype and its tank, so the two rows carrying the\\nsame colony label are repeated measurements of the same coral rather than\\nseparate corals.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input data contain exactly 6 colonies with 2 rows each; e.g., colony CL01 contributes two nubbin rows under the same ambient regime.\",\"observed_value\":\"12 rows, 6 unique colony_id values, 2 rows per colony\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":3,\"quoted_text\":\"CL01,ambient,CL01N1,18.4,13.0\\nCL01,ambient,CL01N2,17.9,13.0\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow builds the two test samples by appending every row's rate keyed only on thermal_regime, so both nubbins of each colony enter the same sample vector.\",\"observed_value\":\"row-level pooling with no aggregation by colony_id\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":26,\"end_line\":32,\"quoted_text\":\"def rates_by_regime(table):\\n    collected = {name: [] for name in REGIMES}\\n    for record in table:\\n        collected[record[REGIME_COLUMN]].append(float(record[RATE_COLUMN]))\\n    return {\\n        name: np.array(values, dtype=float) for name, values in collected.items()\\n    }\"}]},{\"description\":\"The row-level vectors are passed directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind with equal_var=True, a procedure whose validity requires each entry to be an independent observation.\",\"observed_value\":\"stats.ttest_ind(ambient, heated, equal_var=True) on 6+6 nubbin rows\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":69,\"end_line\":71,\"quoted_text\":\"    outcome = stats.ttest_ind(ambient, heated, equal_var=True)\\n    t_stat = float(outcome.statistic)\\n    p_value = float(outcome.pvalue)\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's selected result claims a significant difference with t(10) and p = 0.0133, based on the 12 nubbin rows.\",\"observed_value\":\"t(10) = 3.0000, p = 0.0133, 95% CI 0.7719 to 5.2281\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Two-sample Student t-test comparing the 12 nubbin calcification measurements between thermal regimes: ambient nubbins calcified 3.000 mg CaCO3 g^-1 d^-1 faster than heated nubbins, t(10) = 3.0000, p = 0.0133 (two-sided, 95% CI 0.7719 to 5.2281).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's interpretation confirms all 12 rows (2 nubbins per colony) were used as the test's observations, which is exactly the repeated entry of each independent unit into the row-independent procedure.\",\"observed_value\":\"all 12 rows used as observations, yielding 10 degrees of freedom\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":29,\"end_line\":31,\"quoted_text\":\"At the 0.05 level the ambient-heated difference in net calcification is\\nstatistically significant. The 12 analysed rows are the 2 nubbins measured\\non each of the 6 parent colonies, and the test used all 12 rows as its\\nobservations, which is where its 10 degrees of freedom come from.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The report is transparent about the clustered structure, correctly disclosing that only 6 colonies contributed 2 measurements each; this rules out a data-misreading explanation but does not repair the test's independence assumption.\",\"observed_value\":\"6 parent colonies, 2 measurements each, accurately reported\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":9,\"end_line\":9,\"quoted_text\":\"- 6 parent colonies contributed 2 measurements each.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The descriptive quantities are unaffected by the unit error: the mean difference of 3.000 mg CaCO3 g^-1 d^-1 is identical whether computed from nubbin rows or colony means (colonies are balanced with 2 nubbins each), so the effect direction and magnitude in the report are correct; only the inferential claim (p-value, CI, significance) is invalid.\",\"observed_value\":\"mean difference 3.000 identical under row-level and colony-mean analysis\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":20,\"quoted_text\":\"- Mean difference (ambient - heated): 3.000 mg CaCO3 g^-1 d^-1\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to falsify the issue in two ways. (1) I checked whether the row-level analysis could be defensible, i.e., whether nubbins might legitimately be independent units: the data description forecloses this by stating treatment was applied to whole colonies and that same-colony rows are repeated measurements of the same coral, and it names colony_id as the independent-unit column. (2) I checked materiality by recomputing the identical comparison at the authorized unit: colony means are ambient {13.0, 15.0, 17.0} and heated {10.5, 12.0, 13.5}; a pooled-variance two-sample t-test on these gives pooled variance 3.125, SE 1.4434, t(4) = 2.078, two-sided p ≈ 0.106, 95% CI ≈ (-1.01, 7.01). Since the report's significance claim (p = 0.0133 < 0.05) reverses to non-significance at the correct unit, the falsification fails and the issue stands as material. I also verified the report's own numbers (variances 3.6 and 2.4, pooled variance 3.0, SE 1.0, t = 3.0, p = 0.0133) reproduce from the 12 rows, confirming the reported result is exactly the row-level test rather than some other computation.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-j1-reviewer-fable-44","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:68ab4a740a5628e5849f","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","issue_class":"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure","bounded_statement":"Within the supplied files, the report's selected result (two-sample Student t-test, t(10) = 3.0000, p = 0.0133, 95% CI 0.7719 to 5.2281, declared statistically significant at alpha = 0.05) is obtained by entering all 12 nubbin rows as independent observations, even though the data description designates colony_id as the independent unit and states that the two rows per colony are repeated measurements of the same coral. Re-running the same comparison on the 6 colony means (the authorized independent units, n = 3 per regime) preserves the mean difference of 3.000 mg CaCO3 g^-1 d^-1 but gives t(4) ≈ 2.078, p ≈ 0.106, 95% CI ≈ -1.01 to 7.01, so the report's significance conclusion is not supported at the declared unit of independence.","root_cause":"The workflow pools rows purely by thermal_regime (rates_by_regime iterates over every CSV record and appends each nubbin's rate) and passes these row-level vectors directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind, a procedure that assumes each entry is an independent observation. The colony_id column is read only to tally rows per colony for reporting, never to aggregate or model the within-colony dependence, so each of the 6 independent units (colonies) enters the row-independent t-test twice, inflating the effective sample size from 6 to 12 and the degrees of freedom from 4 to 10.","evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description names colony_id as the independent-unit column and states one row is a single nubbin measurement from a parent colony.","observed_value":"Independent unit column: colony_id","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":25,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"One row is: one nubbin's net calcification measurement, taken from one parent colony\nIndependent unit column: colony_id"}]},{"description":"The data description explicitly warns that rows sharing a colony label are dependent repeated measurements, with treatment applied at the colony level.","observed_value":"two nubbins per colony share genotype and tank; rows with the same colony label are repeated measurements of the same coral","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":11,"end_line":14,"quoted_text":"The temperature treatment was applied to whole colonies, and the two nubbins from\na colony share that colony's genotype and its tank, so the two rows carrying the\nsame colony label are repeated measurements of the same coral rather than\nseparate corals."}]},{"description":"The input data contain exactly 6 colonies with 2 rows each; e.g., colony CL01 contributes two nubbin rows under the same ambient regime.","observed_value":"12 rows, 6 unique colony_id values, 2 rows per colony","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":3,"quoted_text":"CL01,ambient,CL01N1,18.4,13.0\nCL01,ambient,CL01N2,17.9,13.0"}]},{"description":"The workflow builds the two test samples by appending every row's rate keyed only on thermal_regime, so both nubbins of each colony enter the same sample vector.","observed_value":"row-level pooling with no aggregation by colony_id","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":26,"end_line":32,"quoted_text":"def rates_by_regime(table):\n    collected = {name: [] for name in REGIMES}\n    for record in table:\n        collected[record[REGIME_COLUMN]].append(float(record[RATE_COLUMN]))\n    return {\n        name: np.array(values, dtype=float) for name, values in collected.items()\n    }"}]},{"description":"The row-level vectors are passed directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind with equal_var=True, a procedure whose validity requires each entry to be an independent observation.","observed_value":"stats.ttest_ind(ambient, heated, equal_var=True) on 6+6 nubbin rows","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":69,"end_line":71,"quoted_text":"    outcome = stats.ttest_ind(ambient, heated, equal_var=True)\n    t_stat = float(outcome.statistic)\n    p_value = float(outcome.pvalue)"}]},{"description":"The report's selected result claims a significant difference with t(10) and p = 0.0133, based on the 12 nubbin rows.","observed_value":"t(10) = 3.0000, p = 0.0133, 95% CI 0.7719 to 5.2281","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Two-sample Student t-test comparing the 12 nubbin calcification measurements between thermal regimes: ambient nubbins calcified 3.000 mg CaCO3 g^-1 d^-1 faster than heated nubbins, t(10) = 3.0000, p = 0.0133 (two-sided, 95% CI 0.7719 to 5.2281)."}]},{"description":"The report's interpretation confirms all 12 rows (2 nubbins per colony) were used as the test's observations, which is exactly the repeated entry of each independent unit into the row-independent procedure.","observed_value":"all 12 rows used as observations, yielding 10 degrees of freedom","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":29,"end_line":31,"quoted_text":"At the 0.05 level the ambient-heated difference in net calcification is\nstatistically significant. The 12 analysed rows are the 2 nubbins measured\non each of the 6 parent colonies, and the test used all 12 rows as its\nobservations, which is where its 10 degrees of freedom come from."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The report is transparent about the clustered structure, correctly disclosing that only 6 colonies contributed 2 measurements each; this rules out a data-misreading explanation but does not repair the test's independence assumption.","observed_value":"6 parent colonies, 2 measurements each, accurately reported","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":9,"end_line":9,"quoted_text":"- 6 parent colonies contributed 2 measurements each."}]},{"description":"The descriptive quantities are unaffected by the unit error: the mean difference of 3.000 mg CaCO3 g^-1 d^-1 is identical whether computed from nubbin rows or colony means (colonies are balanced with 2 nubbins each), so the effect direction and magnitude in the report are correct; only the inferential claim (p-value, CI, significance) is invalid.","observed_value":"mean difference 3.000 identical under row-level and colony-mean analysis","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":20,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"- Mean difference (ambient - heated): 3.000 mg CaCO3 g^-1 d^-1"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to falsify the issue in two ways. (1) I checked whether the row-level analysis could be defensible, i.e., whether nubbins might legitimately be independent units: the data description forecloses this by stating treatment was applied to whole colonies and that same-colony rows are repeated measurements of the same coral, and it names colony_id as the independent-unit column. (2) I checked materiality by recomputing the identical comparison at the authorized unit: colony means are ambient {13.0, 15.0, 17.0} and heated {10.5, 12.0, 13.5}; a pooled-variance two-sample t-test on these gives pooled variance 3.125, SE 1.4434, t(4) = 2.078, two-sided p ≈ 0.106, 95% CI ≈ (-1.01, 7.01). Since the report's significance claim (p = 0.0133 < 0.05) reverses to non-significance at the correct unit, the falsification fails and the issue stands as material. I also verified the report's own numbers (variances 3.6 and 2.4, pooled variance 3.0, SE 1.0, t = 3.0, p = 0.0133) reproduce from the 12 rows, confirming the reported result is exactly the row-level test rather than some other computation.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":31386,"ttft_stream_ms":1459,"time_to_request_ms":10,"type":"result","duration_ms":69808,"uuid":"56c6ff92-b2ec-4cfc-a735-bf45d957f9aa"}
